Stiff-Man Syndrome in a Child 
The stiff-man syndrome (SMS) is a neurologic disorder char- 
acterized by persistent rigidity and stiffness mainly in the axial 
musculature, with superimposed fluctuating severe, often pain- 
ful, muscle spasms. This condition is associated with an elec- 
