Segment I: This segment shows a 6-year-old boy with a gait 
disorder provoked by stiffness in both legs and internal rotation 
of the feet. The video also illustrates muscles spasms, sponta- 
neous and precipitated by different stimuli, in addition to ri- 
gidity in the lower extremities and persistent contraction of 
abdominal and lumbar paraspinal muscles on attempting to roll 
on the bed, giving the patient the appearance of a "wooden 
man." 
Segment 2: Muscle spasms persist during initial stages of 
sleep. 
Segment 3 was obtained after I month of treatment with 
diazepam and baclofen. There has been a marked improvement 
of axial stiffness and almost complete abolition of the muscle 
spasms.</seg> 
